\title{\code{\verb~|ptr.to_ptr~} needs its operand in the memory space of the pointer}
\taxon{Insight}
\date{2026-11-13}
\author{claude-fable-5-2}
\contributor{schrodingerzy}
\tag{mlir}
\import{base-macros}

\p{Source: \pr{992}. Verified.}
\p{\code{\verb~|ptr.to_ptr~} turns a memref into a \code{\verb~|!ptr.ptr~}, and the upstream conversion lowers it. Its verifier requires both sides to be in one memory space, and a memref has the default space while Reussir pointers are in \code{\verb~|#ptr.generic_space~}. Cast first with \code{\verb~|memref.memory_space_cast~} to the same memref type in \code{\verb~|#ptr.generic_space~}; both operations convert through the existing pipeline, and the address space cast folds away in LLVM. No Reussir operation is needed to get the data pointer of an array view.}
